png_struct = core::mem::zeroed();`\n  and remember the C code then does `*png_ptr = create_struct;` — translate that\n  as `core::ptr::write(png_ptr, create_struct);`.\n- `png_info_init_3` compares `png_info_struct_size != sizeof(png_info)` -> use\n  `core::mem::size_of::<png_info>()`.\n- In png_free_data the `#ifdef` chain covers PNG_FREE_TEXT, PNG_FREE_SPLT,\n  PNG_FREE_UNKN, PNG_FREE_HIST, PNG_FREE_PLTE, PNG_FREE_TRNS, PNG_FREE_SCAL,\n  PNG_FREE_PCAL, PNG_FREE_ICCP, PNG_FREE_EXIF, PNG_FREE_ROWS - all are enabled.\n\nRules recap:\n- non-static C function -> `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn <exact C name>(...)`\n- static C function -> `unsafe fn name(...)` (module-private), or `unsafe extern \"C\" fn name(...)` if its address is taken.\n- NO `use`, NO `mod`, NO `#![...]` lines in the part file.\n- Reproduce behaviour EXACTLY: same order of checks, same arithmetic, same error strings.\n- Keep the C comments for traceability.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE FINISHING\nRun:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-rKwhA5/translated_rust && cargo build --release --target-dir target/a_png_c_p01 2>&1 | grep -B3 -A10 \"png_c_p01.rs\" | head -250\nFix every error located in YOUR file, EXCEPT `E0425 cannot find function/value` for\nlibpng functions (`png_*`) that are defined in other, not-yet-translated part files -\nthose are expected. Iterate until only such expected errors remain.\n\nREPORT: the list of functions you translated and the output of `wc -l src/gen/png_c_p01.rs`."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4288,"cache_read_input_tokens":338671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4288,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9f98909-8564-4f94-b720-603696df3aad","uuid":"d94c6c3c-a38f-41dc-afce-ba95b086fb45","timestamp":"2026-08-22T19:58:52.603Z"}
