S_SUPPORTED\n287\tPNG_MIPS_*  PNG_POWERPC_*  PNG_RISCV_*  PNG_LOONGARCH_*  PNG_INTEL_SSE_*\n288\tPNG_USER_CONFIG  PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K  PNG_SMALL_SIZE_T\n289\tPNG_FIXED_POINT_MACRO_SUPPORTED  PNG_DEBUG  PNG_PREFIX\n290\tPNG_READ_BIG_ENDIAN_SUPPORTED   PNG_ARM_NEON_IMPLEMENTATION (== 0)\n291\tPNG_RISCV_RVV_IMPLEMENTATION (== 0)\n292\t```\n293\t\n294\t`PNG_ARM_NEON_OPT`, `PNG_MIPS_*_OPT`, `PNG_POWERPC_VSX_OPT`,\n295\t`PNG_INTEL_SSE_IMPLEMENTATION`, `PNG_LOONGARCH_LSX_IMPLEMENTATION`,\n296\t`PNG_RISCV_RVV_IMPLEMENTATION`, `PNG_MIPS_MSA_IMPLEMENTATION` are all `0`.\n297\t`PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS` is **not** defined.\n298\t`PNG_LIBPNG_VER` is `10659` (so `#if PNG_LIBPNG_VER < 10700` is taken).\n299\t`PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is **false** (`PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE` == BETA == 2 <\n300\tRC == 3), so `#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` branches are **not** taken.\n301\t`PNG_USE_COMPILE_TIME_MASKS` is `1`.\n302\t`PNG_sRGB_PROFILE_CHECKS` is `2`.\n303\t`PNG_USE_READ_MACROS` **is** defined.\n304\t\n305\t## Diverging functions\n306\t\n307\t`png_error`, `png_chunk_error`, `png_longjmp`, `png_fixed_error` and\n308\t`png_safe_error` are declared `-> !` in Rust.  Code after a call to them is\n309\tunreachable; that is fine (the `unreachable_code` lint is allowed).  If a\n310\tfunction must return a value and every path ends in `png_error`, no `return` is\n311\tneeded.\n312\t\n313\t`png_benign_error`, `png_chunk_benign_error`, `png_app_error` return `()`.\n314\t\n315\t## Floating point\n316\t\n317\t`pow`, `floor`, `ceil`, `fabs`, `log`, `exp`, `modf`, `frexp` are declared in\n318\t`src/ffi.rs` as the C library functions — call them directly (do **not** use\n319\tRust's `f64::powf` etc., to guarantee identical results).  `DBL_DIG`,\n320\t`DBL_MIN`, `DBL_MAX` are available.\n321\t\n322\t## Checklist before finishing\n323\t\n324\t1. Only the functions in your assigned line range, in the same order.\n325\t2. Every non-`static` C function has `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn`\n326\t   with the exact C symbol name.\n327\t3. No `use`/`mod`/`#![..]` lines in a part file.\n328\t4. No `unsafe { }` blocks needed (bodies of `unsafe fn` are implicitly unsafe).\n329\t5. Comments from the C source are worth keeping for traceability.\n330\t\n331\t---\n332\t\n333\t## Your workflow (sub-agent instructions)\n334\t\n335\tProject dir (`cd` here for all commands):\n336\t`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-rKwhA5/translated_rust`\n337\t\n338\t1. Read this whole file.\n339\t2. Read `src/pngerror.rs`, `src/pngmem.rs`, `src/gen/png_c_p01.rs` — finished\n340\t   reference translations.  Match their style exactly.\n341\t3. Read `src/pngtypes.rs` and `src/util.rs` so you use the correct struct field\n342\t   names, type aliases and helper names.\n343\t4. Read the module header `src/<MOD>.rs` for your C file: it already declares the\n344\t   file-scope constants / types / data tables.  **Do NOT redefine them.**\n345\t5. Read your assigned C line range with the `Read` tool (`offset`/`limit`) and\n346\t   write the translation of **every function whose definition begins in that\n347\t   range** into your assigned `src/gen/<MOD>_pNN.rs`, overwriting the placeholder.\n348\t   Nothing else goes in that file.\n349\t6. Verify:\n350\t   ```\n351\t   cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-rKwhA5/translated_rust \\\n352\t     && cargo build --release --target-dir target/<your unique dir> 2>&1 \\\n353\t        | grep -B3 -A10 \"<MOD>_pNN.rs\" | head -250\n354\t   ```\n355\t   Fix every error located in **your** file, except `E0425 cannot find\n356\t   function/value <png_...>` for libpng functions that live in other,\n357\t   not-yet-translated part files — those are expected.  Repeat until only such\n358\t   expected errors remain.  Do not edit any file other than your own part file.\n359\t7. Report the list of functions translated and `wc -l` of your file.\n360\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DbLLkaMvMqHUFHMgo4QSED","session_id":"d9f98909