end`'s trailer-text loop uses `>= PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt` for the compressed branch (differs from `png_write_info`'s `==` in p01) — reproduced verbatim.\n- Integer promotion preserved in `png_do_write_intrapixel`: 8-bit path computes differences in `c_int` before truncating to `png_byte`; 16-bit path builds `s0/s1/s2` as `(( *rp as c_int) << 8) as png_uint_32 | ...` and uses `wrapping_sub` before the `& 0xffff` mask.\n- `num_palette_max >= num_palette` compared with an explicit `as c_int` cast on the `png_uint_16` field.\n\nVerification: `cargo build --release --target-dir target/a_pngwrite_p02` yields exactly two errors located in this file, both `E0425 cannot find function png_write_row` (lines 257 and 290). `png_write_row` begins at pngwrite.c line 746, i.e. it belongs to the next chunk (`pngwrite_p03.rs`, still a placeholder), so these are the expected cross-part errors. No other errors or warnings reference `pngwrite_p02.rs`, and no files other than my part file were modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":54423,"tool_uses":15,"duration_ms":157212},"uuid":"a7c30fc9-6f45-497e-80d8-d358ce80cc93","session_id":"d9f98909-8564-4f94-b720-603696df3aad"}
