ng in for C's uninitialized local.\n- `--png_ptr->user_chunk_cache_max == 1` split into a `wrapping_sub` assignment followed by the comparison.\n- `entry_start - buffer` -> `entry_start.offset_from(buffer) as png_uint_32`; `PNG_SIZE_MAX / sizeof(png_sPLT_entry)` uses `core::mem::size_of::<png_sPLT_entry>()`.\n- Every `png_crc_finish`, `png_chunk_benign_error`, `png_chunk_warning` and `png_warning` message reproduced verbatim (\"too short\", \"bad keyword\", \"bad compression method\", \"extra compressed data\", \"out of memory\", \"malformed sPLT chunk\", \"sPLT chunk has bad length\", \"sPLT chunk too long\", \"sPLT chunk requires too much memory\", \"No space in chunk cache for sPLT\").\n\nVerification: `cargo build --release --target-dir target/a_pngrutil_p04` produces zero errors or warnings referencing `pngrutil_p04.rs`. The only remaining build errors are the 9 expected `E0425 cannot find function` for libpng functions living in not-yet-translated part files (`png_destroy_read_struct`, `png_handle_chunk`, `png_handle_unknown`, `png_read_filter_row`, `png_do_read_transformations`, `png_do_read_interlace`, `png_combine_row`), all located in `png_c_p10.rs`, `pngpread_p01.rs` and `pngpread_p02.rs`. No files other than my part file were modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":66439,"tool_uses":18,"duration_ms":161569},"uuid":"8745f574-7c9d-4bca-8352-b3e27e765e93","session_id":"d9f98909-8564-4f94-b720-603696df3aad"}
