{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013kwssw6rkoKGFwg6sQi1op","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# libpng C -> Rust translation conventions\n2\t\n3\tRead this file **completely** before translating anything.  Every translated\n4\tfile must follow these rules exactly so that the pieces fit together.\n5\t\n6\t## Goal\n7\t\n8\tA *mechanical*, behaviour-identical transliteration of libpng 1.6.59 C code into\n9\t`unsafe` Rust.  **Do not** refactor, \"improve\", fix bugs, reorder checks, or\n10\tchange arithmetic.  The resulting shared library must produce byte-identical\n11\toutput to the C library.\n12\t\n13\t## Where code goes\n14\t\n15\tEach C file `c_src/src/<x>.c` maps to a Rust module.  Large C files are split\n16\tinto \"part\" files which are `include!`d into the module, so **all parts of one\n17\tC file share a single Rust module scope**:\n18\t\n19\t| C file        | Rust module file  | part files                 |\n20\t|---------------|-------------------|----------------------------|\n21\t| png.c         | `src/png_c.rs`    | `src/gen/png_c_pNN.rs`     |\n22\t| pngerror.c    | `src/pngerror.rs` | (already done)             |\n23\t| pngget.c      | `src/pngget.rs`   | `src/gen/pngget_pNN.rs`    |\n24\t| ...           | ...               | ...                        |\n25\t\n26\t**A part file must contain only items (functions, `static`s, `const`s, `struct`s).\n27\tIt must NOT contain `use` statements, `mod` statements, or inner attributes**\n28\t(`#![...]`); the enclosing module file already has `use crate::*;` and the crate\n29\troot has all the `#![allow(...)]` lint attributes.\n30\t\n31\tEverything from `src/pngtypes.rs`, `src/util.rs`, `src/ffi.rs` and every other\n32\tmodule is in scope automatically via `use crate::*;`.\n33\t\n34\t## Function signatures\n35\t\n36\t* Every function that is **not** `static` in C becomes:\n37\t\n38\t  ```rust\n39\t  #[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n40\t  pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn png_foo(a: png_structrp, b: c_int) -> png_uint_32 {\n41\t  ```\n42\t\n43\t  The `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` attribute is mandatory and the symbol name must be\n44\t  exactly the C name.\n45\t\n46\t* Every function that **is** `static` in C becomes a module-private Rust fn:\n47\t\n48\t  ```rust\n49\t  unsafe fn png_foo(a: png_structrp) -> c_int {\n50\t  ```\n51\t\n52\t  *Exception*: a `static` C function whose address is taken (stored in a\n53\t  function pointer, e.g. the row filter functions or `png_image_read_*`\n54\t  callbacks) must be `unsafe extern \"C\" fn` (no `#[no_mangle]`, not `pub`):\n55\t\n56\t  ```rust\n57\t  unsafe extern \"C\" fn png_read_filter_row_sub(\n58\t      row_info: png_row_infop, row: png_bytep, prev_row: png_const_bytep) {\n59\t  ```\n60\t\n61\t* Use the libpng type aliases (`png_structrp`, `png_bytep`, `png_uint_32`,\n62\t  `png_const_charp`, `c_int`, `usize`, ...) exactly as they appear in the C\n63\t  prototype.  `size_t` -> `usize`, `int` -> `c_int`, `unsigned int` -> `c_uint`,\n64\t  `double` -> `f64`, `float` -> `f32`, `char` -> `c_char`, `png_byte` ->\n65\t  `png_byte`.\n66\t\n67\t* `png_const_structrp`, `png_const_structp`, `png_const_inforp`,\n68\t  `png_const_infop` are all aliases for **mutable** pointers\n69\t  (`*mut png_struct` / `*mut png_info`), so `png_constcast(png_structrp, png_ptr)`\n70\t  is simply `png_ptr`.\n71\t\n72\t* Since the fn is `unsafe fn`, the whole body is an implicit unsafe block\n73\t  (crate edition is 2021).  Do **not** wrap things in `unsafe { }`.\n74\t\n75\t## Pointers\n76\t\n77\t* `NULL` -> `core::ptr::null_mut()` for `*mut T`, `core::ptr::null()` for\n78\t  `*const T`.  Comparisons: `p != core::ptr::null_mut()`, or `p.is_null()` /\n79\t  `!p.is_null()` — either is fine, be consistent within a function.\n80\t* `p[i]` -> `*p.add(i)` when `i` is `usize`, or `*p.offset(i as isize)` when `i`\n81\t  may be signed.  For **writes**: `*p.add(i) = v;`\n82\t* `*p++` (read then advance) ->\n83\t  ```rust\n84\t  let v = *sp; sp = sp.add(1);\n85\t  ```\n86\t  `*--p` (advance then read/write) ->\n87\t  ```rust\n88\t  sp = sp.sub(1); let v = *sp;\n89\t  ```\n90\t* `p + n` -> `p.add(n)` / `p.offset(n as isize)`; `p - n` -> `p.sub(n)`.\n91\t* Pointer difference `p - q` -> `p.offset_from(q)` (gives `isize`).\n92\t* Casting between pointer types is a plain `as`:\n93\t  `data as *mut c_void`, `p as *const c_char`, `q as png_bytep`.\n94\t* `png_voidcast(type, value)`, `png_aligncast`, `png_aligncastconst` -> `value as <type>`.\n95\t* Taking the address of a struct field: `core::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*png_ptr).zstream)`\n96\t  (or `&mut (*png_ptr).zstream` — prefer `addr_of_mut!` for fields of a `*mut`).\n97\t\n98\t## Struct field access\n99\t\n100\t`png_ptr->mode` -> `(*png_ptr).mode`.  `info_ptr->text[i].key` ->\n101\t`(*(*info_ptr).text.add(i)).key`.\n102\t\n103\t## Function pointer fields and parameters\n104\t\n105\tAll C function-pointer types are `Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(..)>` in Rust\n106\t(see `src/pngtypes.rs`).  Therefore:\n107\t\n108\t| C                                | Rust                                     |\n109\t|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------|\n110\t| `png_ptr->error_fn != NULL`      | `(*png_ptr).error_fn.is_some()`           |\n111\t| `png_ptr->error_fn == NULL`      | `(*png_ptr).error_fn.is_none()`           |\n112\t| `png_ptr->error_fn = NULL`       | `(*png_ptr).error_fn = None`               |\n113\t| `png_ptr->error_fn = my_fn`      | `(*png_ptr).error_fn = Some(my_fn)`        |\n114\t| `(*(png_ptr->error_fn))(a, b)`   | `((*png_ptr).error_fn.unwrap())(a, b)`     |\n115\t| parameter `png_error_ptr fn`     | `fn_: png_error_ptr` (already an `Option`) |\n116\t\n117\t`png_ptr->read_filter[i]` has type `png_read_filter_fn`\n118\t(`Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(png_row_infop, png_bytep, png_const_bytep)>`).\n119\t\n120\t## String literals\n121\t\n122\tC string literals become NUL-terminated byte strings cast to a pointer:\n123\t\n124\t```rust\n125\tpng_error(png_ptr, b\"Out of memory\\0\".as_ptr() as png_const_charp);\n126\t```\n127\t\n128\tAdjacent C literals `\"a\" \"b\"` are one Rust literal `b\"ab\\0\"`.\n129\tA `char` literal `'x'` is `b'x' as c_char` (or just the numeric value).\n130\t\n131\t## Control flow\n132\t\n133\t* `for (i = 0; i < n; i++) { body }` becomes\n134\t  ```rust\n135\t  let mut i = 0; // or the C type\n136\t  while i < n {\n137\t      body\n138\t      i += 1;\n139\t  }\n140\t  ```\n141\t  **If `body` contains `continue`, you must place the increment before every\n142\t  `continue`**, or restructure with a labelled block:\n143\t  ```rust\n144\t  while i < n {\n145\t      'cont: {\n146\t          ... break 'cont; ...   // replaces `continue`\n147\t      }\n148\t      i += 1;\n149\t  }\n150\t  ```\n151\t* `do { body } while (c);` -> `loop { body; if !(c) { break; } }`\n152\t* `while (c) body` -> `while c { body }`\n153\t* `switch (x) { case A: ...; break; case B: ... }` -> `match x { A => {...}, B => {...}, _ => {} }`\n154\t  Consts can be used as match patterns.  **Fall-through** must be made explicit\n155\t  by duplicating the shared code into each arm (see `png_format_number` in\n156\t  `src/pngerror.rs` for an example).  A `switch` with no `default` needs\n157\t  `_ => {}`.\n158\t* `goto label` where `label` is *forward* and at the end of an enclosing block:\n159\t  wrap the region in a labelled block and use `break 'label;`.\n160\t* Ternary `c ? a : b` -> `if c { a } else { b }`.\n161\t* `if (x)` where `x` is an integer -> `if x != 0`; `if (!x)` -> `if x == 0`.\n162\t  For pointers -> `if !x.is_null()` / `if x.is_null()`.\n163\t* Comma expressions and assignments-in-expressions must be rewritten as\n164\t  statements.\n165\t\n166\t## Arithmetic\n167\t\n168\t* The crate is built with `overflow-checks = false`, so `+ - *` wrap like C's\n169\t  unsigned arithmetic.  Still, prefer `wrapping_add` / `wrapping_sub` /\n170\t  `wrapping_mul` / `wrapping_neg` when the C code is *known* to rely on\n171\t  wrap-around, and always use them for `png_uint_32`/`png_uint_16` expressions\n172\t  that could overflow.  **Never** introduce a panic path.\n173\t* Watch out for C integer promotion: `png_byte a, b; a - b` is computed in\n174\t  `int`.  Translate as `(a as c_int) - (b as c_int)`.\n175\t* Shifts: C `x << n` on a `png_byte` promotes to int.  Use\n176\t  `((x as c_int) << n)` then cast back.\n177\t* `(png_byte)x` -> `x as png_byte` etc.  Rust `as` on integers truncates just\n178\t  like C.\n179\t* Division/modulo by a value that could be 0 must be reproduced verbatim (the C\n180\t  code never does this on a valid path).\n181\t* `abs(x)` -> `abs(x)` (helper in `util.rs`, takes/returns `c_int`).\n182\t\n183\t## Available helpers (from `src/util.rs`)\n184\t\n185\t`memcpy(dst, src, n)`, `memmove`, `memset(dst, v, n)`, `memcmp(a, b, n)` all\n186\ttake `*mut c_void` / `*const c_void`, so add `as *mut c_void` /\n187\t`as *const c_void` casts.  `strlen(s: *const c_char) -> usize`, `strcmp`,\n188\t`strncmp`.\n189\t\n190\tMacros translated as functions (same names unless noted):\n191\t\n192\t* `PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_bits, width)` — both args `usize`, returns `usize`.\n193\t* `PNG_TRAILBITS`, `PNG_PADBITS`, `PNG_DIV65535`, `PNG_DIV257`,\n194\t  `PNG_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `PNG_COLOR_DIST`, `png_float`.\n195\t* **`png_get_uint_32(buf)` / `png_get_uint_16(buf)` / `png_get_int_32(buf)` are\n196\t  MACROS inside the library.  Inside translated code call\n197\t  `PNG_get_uint_32(buf)`, `PNG_get_uint_16(buf)`, `PNG_get_int_32(buf)`**\n198\t  (the identically-named exported functions live in `pngrutil.rs`).\n199\t* `PNG_CHUNK_FROM_STRING(s)`, `PNG_STRING_FROM_CHUNK(s, c)`,\n200\t  `PNG_CSTRING_FROM_CHUNK(s, c)`, `PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY(c)`,\n201\t  `PNG_CHUNK_CRITICAL(c)` (returns `bool`), `PNG_CHUNK_PRIVATE(c)`,\n202\t  `PNG_CHUNK_RESERVED(c)`, `PNG_CHUNK_SAFE_TO_COPY(c)`,\n203\t  `PNG_CHUNK_NAME_VALID(c)` (returns `bool`).\n204\t* `png_chunk_flag_from_index(i)`, `png_file_has_chunk(png_ptr, i)` (`bool`),\n205\t  `png_file_add_chunk(png_ptr, i)`.  `png_has_chunk(png_ptr, cHNK)` ->\n206\t  `png_file_has_chunk(png_ptr, PNG_INDEX_cHNK)`.\n207\t* `png_chunk_max(png_ptr)`.\n208\t* `PNG_PASS_START_ROW/START_COL/ROW_OFFSET/COL_OFFSET/ROW_SHIFT/COL_SHIFT(pass:\n209\t  c_int) -> c_int`, `PNG_PASS_ROWS/COLS(v: png_uint_32, pass: c_int)`,\n210\t  `PNG_ROW_FROM_PASS_ROW`, `PNG_COL_FROM_PASS_COL`, `PNG_PASS_MASK(pass, off)`,\n211\t  `PNG_ROW_IN_INTERLACE_PASS(y, pass)`, `PNG_COL_IN_INTERLACE_PASS(x, pass)`.\n212\t* `png_composite(fg, alpha, bg) -> png_byte` and\n213\t  `png_composite_16(fg, alpha, bg) -> png_uint_16` **return** the composite\n214\t  instead of assigning it, so\n215\t  `png_composite(*dp, *sp, alpha, bg)` becomes `*dp = png_composite(...)`.\n216\t  Arguments must be cast to `png_uint_16` / `png_uint_32` respectively.\n217\t* `PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(linear)` is in `png_c.rs`; call it as a normal fn.\n218\t* `PNG_IMAGE_*` size macros take `fmt: png_uint_32` or `image: *const png_image`\n219\t  — see `src/util.rs`.\n220\t* `PNG_ABORT()` -> `PNG_ABORT()`.\n221\t* `PNG_UNUSED(x)`, `png_debug*(...)` -> delete the line entirely.\n222\t\n223\t## Local arrays / structs\n224\t\n225\t```c\n226\tpng_byte buf[13];\n227\t```\n228\t```rust\n229\tlet mut buf: [png_byte; 13] = [0; 13];\n230\t```\n231\tPass as `buf.as_mut_ptr()` / `buf.as_ptr()`.  `sizeof buf` -> the constant size.\n232\t\n233\t```c\n234\tpng_color_16 my_background;\n235\t```\n236\t```rust\n237\tlet mut my_background: png_color_16 = Default::default(); // == {0}\n238\t```\n239\t`png_row_info`, `png_color`, `png_color_8`, `png_color_16`, `png_sPLT_entry`,\n240\t`png_time`, `png_xy`, `png_XYZ` all implement `Default` and `Copy`.\n241\t`png_text`, `png_unknown_chunk`, `png_sPLT_t` are `Copy` but not `Default`\n242\t(they contain pointers) — build them field by field or with a struct literal.\n243\t\n244\tStruct assignment `*a = *b;` -> `*a = *b;` works for `Copy` structs;\n245\tfor