rt, left: png_byte, right: png_byte }`.\n  `png_malloc_warn(png_ptr, size_of::<png_dsort>())` etc.\n* This is a long colour-quantisation routine with three phases; reproduce every\n  loop, every `png_malloc`/`png_free`, the `PNG_COLOR_DIST` usage, and the\n  bit-shift index arithmetic (`PNG_QUANTIZE_RED_BITS` etc. are 5) EXACTLY.\n* `PNG_COLOR_DIST(c1, c2)` is a fn in src/util.rs taking two `png_color` VALUES\n  and returning `c_int` (so pass `*p1`, `*p2` or the struct values).\n* Watch out for `continue` inside `for` loops - see TRANSLATION_NOTES.md.\n* `num_red`/`num_green`/`num_blue`/`num_entries` and the `distance` array\n  allocation sizes must match exactly.","agentId":"ac4c6373c2f775582","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Verified with `cargo build --release --target-dir target/a_pngrtran_p02` — grepping for `pngrtran_p02.rs` in the build output produces **nothing** (no errors or warnings attributed to my file). The only remaining crate errors are the expected `E0425 cannot find function` for libpng functions living in not-yet-translated part files: `png_destroy_read_struct`, `png_do_read_transformations`, `png_init_read_transformations`.\n\nFunctions translated (all of `c_src/src/pngrtran.c` lines 489..892):\n- `png_set_quantize` -> `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn png_set_quantize(png_structrp, png_colorp, c_int, c_int, png_const_uint_16p, c_int)`\n\nOutput file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-rKwhA5/translated_rust/src/gen/pngrtran_p02.rs` — 476 lines.\n\nTranslation details worth noting:\n- All three phases reproduced verbatim: (1) histogram bubble-sort / least-used-color discard with the two `full_quantize` sub-branches and the `PNG_COLOR_DIST` nearest-color search; (2) the no-histogram closest-pair elimination using the 769-entry `png_dsortp` hash chain, including the `t == NULL` early-break propagation, the `if (t != NULL) for (...)` guard, the `num_new_palette & 0x01` left/right