w` + `png_read_transform_info` (READ_TRANSFORMS is enabled) or the duplicate-call `png_app_error`.\n5. `png_start_read_image` — exported. `png_read_start_row` or the duplicate-call `png_app_error`.\n6. `png_do_read_intrapixel` — module-private `unsafe fn` (static in C, address never taken; it is called from `png_read_row` in part 2). Both the 8-bit and 16-bit paths, with C integer-promotion preserved: the 8-bit case computes `(256 + a + b) & 0xff` in `c_int`; the 16-bit case builds `s0/s1/s2` as `((byte as c_int) << 8) as png_uint_32 | byte as png_uint_32` and uses `wrapping_add` for the `+ 65536` sums.\n\nVerification: `cargo build --release --target-dir target/a_pngread_p01` — grepping for `pngread_p01.rs` produces no output, i.e. zero errors or warnings attributed to my file. The only remaining crate error is the expected `E0425: cannot find function png_destroy_read_struct` in `src/gen/png_c_p10.rs`, which lives in a not-yet-translated `pngread.c` part file. No files other than my assigned part file were modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":58150,"tool_uses":17,"duration_ms":145194},"uuid":"9550a22d-9b16-4625-95d7-45a13d60bed4","session_id":"d9f98909-8564-4f94-b720-603696df3aad"}
